#DESCRIPTION
Langmuir test, explicit full PIC (predictor-corrector): a 1D uniform thermal plasma (m_i/m_e = 100) whose E_x noise carries the Langmuir branch; checks energy conservation and the omega-k spectrum against Bohm-Gross. Code units c = 1, n = 1: omega_pe = 35.4, v_te = 0.354, lambda_De = 0.010, dx = 2.8 lambda_De, c dt/dx = 0.36, omega_pe dt = 0.35; 1600 steps (FLEKS issue 170).

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI
1.0e5                   uNormSI

#GEOMETRY
-3.544908               xMin
 3.544908               xMax
-0.0138473              yMin
 0.0138473              yMax
-0.0138473              zMin
 0.0138473              zMax

#NCELL
256                     nCellX   (dx = 0.0277 = 2.8 lambda_De)
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
16                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#FIELDSOLVER
explicit

#FIELDINTEGRATOR
pc                      fieldIntegrator

#FIELDSUBCYCLE
1                       nSubcycle
F                       isAutoSubcycle

#PLASMA
2                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge
0.01                    mass     (m_i/m_e = 100)
-1.0                    charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
65.15939                rho      (n = 1 code)
0.0                     ux
0.0                     uy
0.0                     uz
378.58                  T        (Ti = 3.125e-4 code)
65.15939                rho
0.0                     ux
0.0                     uy
0.0                     uz
1514.3                  T        (Te = 1.25e-3 code)
0.0                     bx
0.0                     by
0.0                     bz
0.0                     ex
0.0                     ey
0.0                     ez

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.01                    dt

Resampling (split/merge) moves particles outside the push and would break
the exact charge conservation that the Gauss's law check tests.
#RESAMPLING
F                       doReSampling

#PARTICLES
64                      nParticle
1                       nParticle
1                       nParticle

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

E_x every 0.04 (4 steps; omega_pe = 35.4 needs < 0.089) for the
omega-k spectrum of the thermal Langmuir noise, and the species densities for
the Gauss's law check.
#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 var ascii pic       plotString
-1                      dn
0.04                    dt
1                       dx
Ex rhoS0 rhoS1          varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
16.0                    TimeMax  (1600 steps)
